{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775350702-xpHuzLkr7ZCxTQmFvC6t","role":"assistant","created":1775350708,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I found the FFO-4 table for 2011. I can see the Social Security Administration row. Looking at the data:\n- Social Security Administration: 155,304 (General funds) + 10 (Management, consolidated, revolving and special funds) + 628,880 (Trust funds) = 784,194 (Total funds)\n\nThis is for FY2011 (the fiscal year ending September 2011). But the task asks for FY2010 to FY2019. \n\nWait, let me re-read the task. It says \"Use FFO-4 tables in December Treasury Bulletins from odd years between 2010 and 2019 to source your data.\"\n\nSo I need to look at:\n- December 2011 Treasury Bulletin (for FY2011 data) - this is the \"This fiscal year to date\" which would be FY2011\n- December 2013 Treasury Bulletin (for FY2013 data)\n- December 2015 Treasury Bulletin (for FY2015 data)\n- December 2017 Treasury Bulletin (for FY2017 data)\n- December 2019 Treasury Bulletin (for FY2019 data)\n\nWait, but the question asks for \"U.S. Federal Social Security Administration nominal budget outlay from FY2010 to FY2019\". That would be 10 years of data. But we only have 5 data points from odd years. \n\nLet me re-read: \"Use FFO-4 tables in December Treasury Bulletins from odd years between 2010 and 2019 to source your data.\"\n\nHmm, this is a bit confusing. The December Treasury Bulletins from odd years (2011, 2013, 2015, 2017, 2019) would give us data for FY2011, FY2013, FY2015, FY2017, and FY2019. But the question asks for FY2010 to FY2019, which is 10 years.\n\nWait, maybe the interpretation is that the December Treasury Bulletin for a given year contains the data for the fiscal year that ended in that calendar year. \n\nI'm puzzling over the exact timing of these fiscal year data points. The December bulletins seem to capture fiscal year data, but there's an inconsistency with the range requested. The fiscal years and calendar years don't align perfectly, which creates ambiguity about which data points to use.\n\nThe \"This fiscal year to date\" column suggests data from the current fiscal year, but the precise mapping isn't clear. I'm noticing a potential mismatch between the requested 10-year period and the available 5-year dataset from odd-numbered years.\n\nThis requires careful interpretation of the fiscal year boundaries and the data representation in the Treasury Bulletins.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_52db0094939840e881eff3d4","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"grep -A 50 \"FFO-4\" /app/resources/treasury_bulletin_2013_12_page_24.txt"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
